# `var opts = options || {}`; what is given is an empty literal that a loop over keys fills. What is seen to arrive at `options` is that literal; the layout with the four names (L3, the literal the loop
# reads from) is only the weakest guess by names. An earlier text asked [L3] first and [L0] on its failing side: the first never passed (433 instructions a turn with options given; 329 now; 122 without).
# What is asked first must be what is written or seen on the other ways; else the body's own literal is asked alone and its failing side is as likely. f1 = configure.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK-NOT: layouts=[L3]
# CHECK: = GetSlotOrUndefined {{*}}key="encoding" receivers=[L0, L1] level=Proven
# CHECK-NOT: layouts=[L3]
# CHECK: Return
# -- source: a-layout-that-only-names-guess-at-is-not-asked-in-front-of-the-own-literal.cjs
